        "object": "<p>Climate experts warn that US Kalshi and Polymarket users are ‘gamifying disasters’ as they bet on events like heatwaves and daily temperatures</p><p>Online prediction markets, saturated by money staked on sport, crypto and politics, have now set their sights on a promising new area of growth: betting on the future livability of the planet itself.</p><p>The rise of gamified predictions on the unfolding climate crisis, and shorter-term weather forecasts, has been underscored by <a href=\"https://news.kalshi.com/p/kalshi-weather-company-partnership\">a new deal</a> that allows Kalshi, a leading online financial exchange, to access data from the Weather Company, owner of the Weather Channel, to verify weather-related betting outcomes.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/sep/02/weather-betting-kalshi-polymarket\">Continue reading...</a>"
